  "goodToKnow": "Nimmer means never, mainly in the fixed phrase nie und nimmer (never ever): Das glaube ich nie und nimmer! In southern Germany and Austria, nimmer is everyday speech for nicht mehr (no longer): Ich mag nimmer (I've had enough). Der Nimmersatt is someone who's never satisfied, and Die kleine Raupe Nimmersatt is the German title of Eric Carle's The Very Hungry Caterpillar. Am Sankt-Nimmerleins-Tag means never."
